We open the door of the neighborhood café right on time.
An older man comes in and walks up to the counter.
"Good morning, what would you like to drink?" I ask politely.
"A cappuccino, please," he says.
I take a deep breath.
The first coffee is always a bit difficult.
I go to the machine and start the espresso.
But the water runs into the cup much too fast.
I get nervous and quickly reach for the milk.
Oh no, I spilled the milk!
The milk drips from the counter onto the floor.
For me, this is a minor disaster.
The customer looks at me in surprise.
"Excuse me, I am still learning to make the coffee," I say quickly.
Elif comes over to me immediately and laughs softly.
"No problem, that happens to almost everyone," she says kindly.
She wipes away the milk and remakes the cappuccino.
The man smiles, pays three euros and takes his drink.
I am very glad that Elif stays so calm.
